    "description": "JAG-79 (Just Another Glock) Frame V1.1: Laffs\n\n\"Just Another Glock\" frame. Does nothing new. For those that just need a basic frame. Doesn't stand out from the tons of other 3DP glock frames, and \nfrankly it's not meant to. No picatinny rail, cuz to be frank, the lot of you don't even have a light on your corpo made pistolas anyway.\n\nVariant of the original Laffs Dynamics JAG-17 frame, the JAG-79 design features a shortened grip section for use of common Glock 19 15rd magazines. \n\n\n\nPrinter Used: Ender 3 V2\n\nFilament Used: PLA+\n\nPrint Settings:\n\nExtruder: 218C\nBed: 56C \nFirst Layer Print Height: .2mm \nStandard Layer Height: .16mm\nWall Perimeters: 8+ \nInfill: 90%+\nSupport Material Percentage: 18%\n\n\n\nParts list and assembly instructions are identical with the DD17.2, and can be found here:\n\nOdysee: https://odysee.com/@TheGatalog-PrintableFramesReceivers:9/FMDA-DD17.2:7\n\n\n\nThe original JAG-17 full sized frame can be found here:\n\nOdysee: https://odysee.com/@LFRF:d/JAG17GlkFrm:0\n\n\n\nRails for this frame can be found here: \n\nAves: https://www.avesrails.com/FMDA-DD172-Rail-Kit-_p_28.html\n\n\n\nAccreditations:\n\nDeterrence Dispensed: Creators of the DD17.2 Used the internals of the DD17.2 frame for the foundation of this design.\n\nAvesRails: Supplied the Glock 17 rail hardware for the design.",
